2
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,000
The Mission is a adventure, drama, action film directed by Roland Joffé.

3
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
When a Spanish Jesuit goes into the South American wilderness to build a mission in the hope of
converting the Indians of the region, a slave hunter is converted and joins his mission.

4
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
When Spain sells the colony to Portugal, they are forced to defend
all they have built against the Portuguese aggressors.

5
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Rodrigo Mendoza, played by Robert De Niro.

6
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Father Gabriel, played by Jeremy Irons.

7
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:51,000
Cardinal Altamirano, played by Ray McAnally.

8
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Felipe Mendoza, played by Aidan Quinn.

9
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Father John Fielding, played by Liam Neeson.

10
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Carlotta, played by Cherie Lunghi.

11
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
The Mission is a 1986 British historical drama film directed by
Roland Joffé, from a screenplay by Robert Bolt.

12
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
It stars Robert De Niro and Jeremy Irons, with Ray McAnally, Aidan
Quinn, Cherie Lunghi and Liam Neeson in supporting roles.

13
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:21,000
It is about the experiences of a Jesuit
missionary in 18th-century South America.

14
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
The film is partly based on Paraguayan saint Roque
González y de Santa Cruz and the Guaraní War.

15
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
The film premiered in competition at the 39th Cannes
Film Festival, winning the Palme d'Or.

16
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
At the 59th Academy Awards, it was nominated for seven awards including Best
Picture and Best Director, winning for Best Cinematography.

17
01:46:15,000 --> 01:46:21,000
The film has also been cited as one of the greatest religious films of all time, appearing in the Vatican film
list's "Religion" section and being number one on the Church Times's Top 50 Religious Films list.

18
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:36,000
The film explores themes of mission, resistance,
christianity, religious conversion, based on true story.

19
01:58:45,000 --> 01:58:51,000
The tone is emotional.
